Package: vale
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: syntax-aware linter for prose
 Vale checks prose against style rules: packaged guides such as Microsoft's
 and Google's, or a project's own rules in .vale.ini and a styles directory.
 It understands Markdown, reStructuredText, AsciiDoc, HTML, and the comments
 and docstrings of most programming languages, so code stays out of the way
 of the prose checks.
 .
 No Ubuntu or Debian archive carries vale and upstream publishes tarballs
 only, so this package builds it. debian/rules clones the release tag
 that debian/changelog names, checks the commit against
 debian/upstream-commit, bumps the two modules whose released versions
 carry advisories, and builds a static binary with a pinned Go toolchain.
 The upstream release binary is not repacked: it carries whatever
 toolchain and module set upstream happened to build with, and those
 accumulate advisories that only a rebuild clears.
